Lemma 6.19(b): the runs of the F4 engine (Lean6.Special.Comp.D88.Count.F4) on the engine inputs kcInputs and
s12Inputs (Comp.D88.Count.Sys), measured 2026-10-17 on a 384-core box, toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0-rc3.

Trusted runs (`lake build <module>`; native_decide evaluates the engine and Comp.Count.dimCheck in compiled code):
  Comp.D88.Count.RunKC   kc_f4_ok  : dimCheck 65521 11 (f4Basis kcCfg kcInputs) 4788 = true
      kcCfg: 11 unknowns, p = 65521, 32 parallel chunks
      lake: Built (32s); wall 0:33.32, user 314 s, max RSS 1,766,736 kB
  Comp.D88.Count.RunS12  s12_f4_ok : dimCheck 65521 11 (f4Basis s12Cfg s12Inputs) 20316 = true
      s12Cfg: 11 unknowns, p = 65521, 64 parallel chunks
      lake: Built (608s); wall 10:08.52, user 11,792 s, max RSS 15,243,004 kB
  Lean6.Special.D88.Count.F4Sound (the soundness theorem f4_good): Built (2.7s)

Development runs of the same engine on the same inputs (Comp.D88.Count.RunDevKC, RunDevS12: a step-by-step driver
with phase timings, not part of the proof; it writes the leading monomials of the active basis elements):
  KC':  53 steps, 31.7 s (32 chunks), max RSS 1,874,580 kB; 4,506 elements added, 2,144 active, 3,249,455 terms;
        largest matrix 56,801 rows x 58,918 columns; 29,071 rows reduced to zero.
  S12:  58 steps, 554.7 s (64 chunks), max RSS 11,947,700 kB; 10,839 elements added, 7,579 active, 43,710,092
        terms; largest matrix 298,465 rows x 309,168 columns; 82,068 rows reduced to zero.
Comparison with msolve 0.9.4 (gen/d88count/f4_cmp_lead.py against the .lead files kc/kc_full_1_2_3_30_p65521.lead
and count/full_1_2_3_30_p65521.lead of rung3/d88/certificates): the minimal leading monomials of the active elements
are exactly msolve's, 2,074 for KC' and 7,411 for S12, and they leave 4,788 and 20,316 standard monomials. The other
active elements (70 and 168) are further elements of the ideal whose leading monomials are multiples of minimal ones;
the dimension check does not need a reduced basis.
For scale: msolve 0.9.4 with 32 threads takes 9.9 s on KC' and 195 s on S12 (logs/d88count/kc_gb_size.log).

The first version of the engine (commit da913f3: the same kinds of trusted operations, with every update of the dense
accumulator reduced modulo p, and a sequential echelon form) gave the same minimal leading monomials in 140 s on KC'
(32 chunks) and 2,403 s on S12 (64 chunks), and its trusted runs passed as well: RunKC built in 140 s (max RSS
1,709,376 kB), RunS12 in 2,474 s (wall 41:14.52, max RSS 16,370,412 kB).

Note (release): the step-by-step development driver used for the development runs and for the comparison of
the leading monomials is not included in the release; the trusted runs above are the modules RunKC and RunS12.
